#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""The parity check of S5 (rule parity: sqll passes 100% of the rule
fixtures, lint and fix; cases that need the Jinja templater move to the
Jinja templater stone).

Design record: docs/decisions/s5-rules.md, sections 3 ("The case classes")
and 4 ("The gap rule"). Task T2 (goal of the task: each rule and autofix
case of the pinned sqlfluff has one class from the data, and the check fails
closed) of S5 made this check.

  uv run --frozen --project harness python scripts/s5/parity \\
      [--root DIR] [--report FILE] [--oracle FILE] [--autofix-oracle FILE] \\
      [--jinja-raw FILE] [--known-failures FILE] [--out FILE] [--exit]

The inputs. A default path is relative to --root (default: the root of this
repository):

  --report          the harness report (default: out/report.json). The check
                    uses the "rules" and "autofix" cases of the tool "sqll".
  --oracle          the output of scripts/sqlfluff-rule-oracle (default:
                    out/oracle.jsonl), one JSON line for each case: {"id",
                    "status", "reason"}.
  --autofix-oracle  the output of scripts/sqlfluff-autofix-oracle (default:
                    out/autofix-oracle.jsonl), in the same format.
  --jinja-raw       the Jinja as raw record (default:
                    results/S3b/C14-jinja-raw.json).
  --known-failures  the known failures of sqll (default:
                    known_failures/sqll.txt).
  fixtures          rules.discover() and autofix.discover() of the harness
                    (harness/sqll_harness/suites/) on
                    <root>/third_party/sqlfluff.
  pinned commit     git rev-parse HEAD:third_party/sqlfluff in <root>.
  submodule         <root>/scripts/check-submodule, and the HEAD of the
                    checkout of the submodule.

The class of each case (design record, section 3). First, the fixture class
comes only from the pinned fixtures and the Jinja as raw record:

  - templater: the templater of the case (rule case: core.templater of its
    configs; autofix case: core.templater of the .sqlfluff file of its
    folder; default jinja) is placeholder or python.
  - jinja: the templater is jinja, and a SQL text has a Jinja tag (a start
    string of the case config; default "{{", "{%", "{#"), or the config has
    a Jinja templater setting (a "templater" section, or core.library_path).
  - other: the templater is raw, or it is jinja and the sha256 of each SQL
    text is in the "equal" list of the Jinja as raw record.
  - no fixture class: each other case (an unknown templater, a jinja text
    with no tag that is not in the record, a case that a note of the record
    names, or a case whose files the check cannot read). Then the case has
    no class.

The SQL texts of a rule case are pass_str, fail_str, and fix_str (only with
a fail_str), as the rules suite writes them. The SQL text of an autofix case
is its before.sql. Then the class:

  "jinja: S11"        the fixture class is jinja (exit: S11, the Jinja
                      templater stone).
  "pass"              sqll passes the case in the report, and the oracle
                      passes it.
  "templater of S6"   the fixture class is templater, and the case is not a
                      pass (exit: this stone, after S6 (templater parity)).
  "gap"               each other case: the fixture class is other and the
                      case is not a pass, or sqll passes the case and the
                      oracle does not.
  no class            the fixture class is not known, the report has no sqll
                      result of the case, the report or the oracle gives
                      "skip", or the oracle output has no line of the case.

Exit code 1 (fail) on each failure of the items below:

  1. Each case has one class: "no_class" (each case with no class),
     "report_extra" and "oracle_extra" (a case id that the fixtures do not
     have).
  2. Each case that sqll passes passes in the oracle: "oracle_mismatch".
  3. The count of each recorded class is the recorded count: "count".
     RECORDED has the counts of the design record, section 3: rules 2527
     cases (fixture classes jinja 169, templater 13), autofix 61 cases
     (jinja 21, templater 0). The check compares the fixture classes,
     because a case of the templater class that sqll passes becomes a pass.
  4. known_failures/sqll.txt has a line for each rules and autofix case that
     sqll does not pass, and no other rules or autofix line:
     "known_failures_missing", "known_failures_stale".
  5. The report sqlfluff_ref and the commit of the Jinja as raw record are
     the pinned commit, and the submodule has no change: "sqlfluff_ref",
     "jinja_raw_commit", "submodule".
  6. With --exit only: no gap (the exit of this stone, design record,
     section 4): "gap" (each case of the class "gap" or "templater of S6").
     With no --exit, the output gives this item with "enforced": false.

Exit code 2 if an input is missing or not valid (the list "errors"). The
check never passes with no data: a report with no sqll case of a suite, an
oracle output with no line, a record with no text, or no fixture case is
not valid.

Output: one JSON object on stdout, and in --out if it is given. It has the
counts of each class for each suite, for each rule file, and for each
autofix dialect ("by_group"), the result of each item, each failure, and
for each case ("cases"): its class, its fixture class, why (the reason of
the fixture class, or of no class), the sqll status of the report, the
oracle status, and if known_failures/sqll.txt has a line of it. The
--recorded option is only for the tests of this check, which use a small
set of fixtures; CI does not give it.
"""

